    <slideshow>
        <title>WeBWorK in <pretext/> in Runestone</title>
        <subtitle>Online Engagement and Assessment</subtitle>

        <frontmatter>
            <titlepage>
                <author>
                    <personname>Chrissy Safranski</personname>
                    <institution>Franciscan University of Steubenville</institution>
                </author>
                <event>JMM 2026</event>
                <date>January 6, 2026</date>
            </titlepage>
        </frontmatter>

        <section>
            <slide>
                <title>Starting with Gratitude</title>

                <sidebyside widths="90%">
                    <p><ul>
                    <li><p>Davide Cervone, Michael Gage, Danny Glin, Alex Jordan,
                        Gavin LaRose, Paul Pearson, Arnold Pizer, John Travis, and many others</p>
                        <p><nbsp/></p>
                    </li>
                    <li><p>Matt Boelkins</p><p><nbsp/></p></li>
                    <li><p>David Austin, Rob Beezer, Tien Chih, Steven Clontz, David Farmer, Oscar Levin, Vilma Mesa, Brad Miller,
                        and many others</p><p><nbsp/></p></li>
                </ul></p>

                </sidebyside>
            </slide>
            <slide>
                <title>Active Learning</title>

                <sidebyside widths="90%">
                    <p><ul pause="yes">
                        <li>
                            <p>
                                <!-- Two unavoidable facts about teaching: active learning is better, and technology is ubiquitous.  Now combine those with
                                the underlying principle that the construction of teaching and learning materials has
                                a strong influence on how the material is taught.  The conclusion is that -->
                                [W]e desperately need textbooks that beyond just supporting active learning, actually induce active learning, and those textbooks should be seamlessly integrated with technology that further supports active learning.
                            </p>
                            <p>
                                --David Farmer, American Institute of Mathematics
                            </p><p><nbsp/></p>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <p>
                                True for more than teaching
                            </p><p><nbsp/></p>
                        <!-- Say here that I want to go even farther than David did - all learning is achieved actively,
                         and interactive course materials are a great asset to helping students learn,
                         even apart from classroom pedagogy.  -->
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <p>
                                Commercial publishers
                            </p>
                        <!-- Many commercial publishers provide textbooks with interactive, autograded homework exercises. -->
                        </li>
                    </ul></p>
                </sidebyside>
            </slide>
            <slide>
                <title>WeBWorK in <pretext/> books</title>
                <sidebyside widths="90%">
                    <p><ul>
                        <li>
                            <p>
                                <url href="https://activecalculus.org/single2e/frontmatter.html">Active Calculus, Single Variable</url>
                            </p>
                            <p><nbsp/></p>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <p>
                                Discrete Mathematics: An Open Introduction
                            </p><p><nbsp/></p>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <p>
                                APEX Calculus
                            </p><p><nbsp/></p>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <p>
                                Open Resources for Community College Algebra (ORCCA)
                            </p>
                        </li>
                    </ul></p>
                </sidebyside>
            </slide>
            <slide>
                <title>Student work, tracked for a grade</title>
                <sidebyside widths="90%">
                    <p><ul>
                        <li>
                            <p>
                                What is Runestone?
                            </p><p><nbsp/></p>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <p>
                                <url href="https://runestone.academy/ns/books/published/ac-single/frontmatter.html?mode=browsing">Active Calculus, Single Variable</url>
                            </p><p><nbsp/></p>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <p>
                                Demo of some WeBWorK problems in Active Calculus in Runestone
                            </p><p><nbsp/></p>
                        </li>
                    </ul></p>
                </sidebyside>
            </slide>
            <slide>
                <title>How?</title>
                <sidebyside widths="90%">
                    <p><ul>
                        <li>
                            <p>
                                Point to an OPL address
                            </p>
                            <p>
                                <sidebyside widths="20% 50%" margins="2% 0%">
                                    <p><url href="https://github.com/Tanaquil18/matrixcalculations/blob/main/source/interactive-exercises/ww-largerinverses.ptx">Source</url></p>
                                    <p><url href="https://tanaquil18.github.io/matrixcalculations/sec-largerinverses.html#ww-largerinverses">Rendered (Ex. 2,3,4)</url></p>
                                </sidebyside>
                            </p>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <p>
                                Written in PreTeXt-WeBWorK
                            </p>
                            <p>
                                <sidebyside widths="10% 40%" margins="2% 0%">
                                    <p><url href="https://github.com/Tanaquil18/matrixcalculations/blob/main/source/interactive-exercises/ww-row-ops.ptx">Source</url></p>
                                    <p><url href="https://tanaquil18.github.io/matrixcalculations/sec-row-ops.html#ww-row-ops">Rendered</url></p>
                                </sidebyside>
                            </p>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <p>
                                Include a local .pg file
                            </p>
                            <p>
                                <sidebyside widths="10% 40%" margins="2% 0%">
                                    <p><url href="https://github.com/Tanaquil18/matrixcalculations/blob/main/source/interactive-exercises/ww-largerinverses.ptx">Source</url></p>
                                    <p><url href="https://tanaquil18.github.io/matrixcalculations/sec-largerinverses.html#ww-largerinverses">Rendered (Ex. 1,5)</url></p>
                                </sidebyside>
                            </p>
                        </li>
                    </ul></p>
                </sidebyside>
            </slide>
            <slide>
                <title>Pros and Cons</title>
                <sidebyside widths="90%">
                    <p><ul>
                        <li>
                            <p>
                                Tightly integrated: notation, language, and learning objectives
                            </p><p><nbsp/></p>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <p>
                                Students like having everything in one place
                            </p><p><nbsp/></p>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <p>
                                Not fully featured
                            </p><p><nbsp/></p>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <p>
                                Much smaller selection of problems
                            </p><p><nbsp/></p>
                        </li>
                    </ul></p>
                </sidebyside>
            </slide>
            <slide>
                <title>Coming Attractions</title>

                <sidebyside widths="90%">
                    <p><ul>
                        <li>
                            <p>
                                Problem bank books
                            </p>
                            <p>
                                <sidebyside widths="10% 40%" margins="0% 0%">
                                    <p><url href="https://github.com/OpenMathBooks/active-calculus-companion/blob/main/source/sec-2-3-prod-quot.xml">Source</url></p>
                                    <p><url href="https://openmathbooks.org/active-calculus-companion/frontmatter.html">Rendered</url></p>
                                </sidebyside>
                            </p><p><nbsp/></p>
                            <!-- Show Active Calculus Companion.
                             Also, an assignment in Runestone containing problems from both ACS and ACC?-->
                        </li>
                    <li><p>STACK</p><p><nbsp/></p>
                    </li>
                    <li><p>Doenet</p><p><nbsp/></p>
                    </li>
                </ul></p>

                </sidebyside>
            </slide>
